# The code-server built-in extensions the editor keeps (docs/code-server.md); every
# other directory under lib/vscode/extensions is deleted when the image is built, so
# a built-in that a later release adds stays out until it is reviewed and listed
# here. Left out on purpose: those that start processes or provide tasks (npm,
# grunt, gulp, jake, php-language-features, terminal-suggest, tunnel-forwarding),
# debugging (ms-vscode.js-debug, ms-vscode.js-debug-companion, debug-auto-launch,
# debug-server-ready), those that render workspace content in same-origin webviews
# (markdown-math, mermaid-markdown-features, ipynb, notebook-renderers,
# ms-vscode.vscode-js-profile-table, simple-browser; markdown-language-features
# stays, with its preview pinned to its Strict policy and its Markdown Editor
# removed by the Dockerfile) and logins
# or outside services (copilot, prompt-basics, github, github-authentication,
# microsoft-authentication, extension-editing), and git: VS Code 1.143's git
# extension asks to trust each repository's folder before opening it, and a
# trusted folder runs its tasks and terminal settings in the editor; git runs
# from the terminal instead, in the shell container.
# One name per line; theme-* keeps every colour and icon theme.
